chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Excel spreadsheets for an advanced course: chapter 14 and today's openpyxl"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-12T16:00:00; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.6." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does chapter 14 of the 3rd edition teach about reading and writing Excel workbooks with openpyxl, which of its printed outputs, programs and files still hold under Python 3.14.6 with the newest openpyxl on 2026-10-12, and what must an advanced course add so that it matches the library as it behaves and the files as they are shipped?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-12." .
